[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` and `c_src/include/lib.h`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are **no runtime option/mode/flag setters** in the API, and no `#ifdef`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `switch`, or `enum` anywhere in the source (verified by grep — see `ERRORS.md`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The axes that the C code genuinely distinguishes are therefore:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Hidden mutable state** — the two file-scope `static int`s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`global_counter`, `global_accumulator`). Three of the entry points read them
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`complex_calc`, `process_pointer_data`, `hatch`) and three write them
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`increment_counter`, `update_accumulator`, `hatch`). So *the same call with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the same arguments returns different values depending on call history*. Every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    row is therefore tested both from a pristine library and from an accumulated
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    state.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Function-pointer dispatch** — `apply_operation(operation_func, ...)` takes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    one of three concrete callees (`add_three`, `multiply_add`, `complex_calc`);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `hatch` also dispatches through `modifier_func`. `complex_calc` additionally
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    couples dispatch to axis 1.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **Shift-vs-size relation** — the guards `shift_by > 0 && shift_by < size`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`shift_array_data`) and `shift > 0 && shift < num_records`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`manipulate_records`) split the input space into "shift applied" and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    "silently skipped". `manipulate_records` splits *again*, because its summation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    loop bound `num_records - shift` is **not** gated by that guard.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **Element count / buffer shape** — `0`, `1`, `many`, and the `malloc`-driven
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    sizes in `compute_with_dynamic_memory(base, count)`; `int` arrays vs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `DataRecord` (48-byte, `time_t`- and `char[32]`-containing) arrays.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **Value magnitude** — small values vs `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` neighbourhoods,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    which selects between plain arithmetic and two's-complement wrap in every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    arithmetic function, and in `get_time_based_value`'s `seed * 3600`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. **Entry-point level** — the header exports only `hatch`, but the `.so`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    exports 11 more lower-level functions. Rows exercise all 11 **directly**, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `hatch` as the composed pipeline, and mixed interleavings of the two.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is driven with many randomized inputs from a fixed-seed PRNG
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`SplitMix64`, seed `0x5EED_1234_ABCD_0001`), not a single hand-picked value.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both `.so`s are always called in identical order so that axis 1 stays in lockstep.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
