The only divergences reported during this work were [1martifacts of my own test harness, not translation bugs[22m. The libraries carry two file-scope [38;5;10mstatic int[0ms ([38;5;10mglobal_counter[0m, [38;5;10mglobal_accumulator[0m) that three functions read and three write, and [38;5;10mdlopen[0m de-duplicates by path — so there is exactly one copy of each static per test process. My first harness assumed a fresh [38;5;10mdlopen[0m gave pristine state and let tests run in parallel, which interleaved mutations of the C and Rust libraries differently and produced 9 spurious failures. Serializing on a mutex and zeroing both libraries' statics before each test (using only exported symbols) made all rows pass. One [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m expectation was also wrong — [38;5;10m(num_records, shift) = (INT_MIN, INT_MAX)[0m wraps the loop bound to [38;5;10m+1[0m rather than negative, so it sums one record; the C was right and the table was corrected.[0m[0m
